    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "This residence was originally constructed circa 1930. It comprises of an entrance porch, living room, 3 bedrooms, a bathroom & a porch at rear with a rear access door.\n\nSubstantial remedial works have been carried out to the roof & chimneys. Further refurbishment and renovation is required. The approach to the property is idyllic in many ways. The hedgerows along the approach road sprout Montbretia and other wildflowers during Spring & Summer. The land which is in a single parcel is at the sides & rear of the residence. Dry outhouses are located beyond the 2 bay hay shed. Old style cart-houses are located immediately adjacent to the cottage. On 0.64ha (1.6 acres) there is an established woodland planted with mixed native species, including oak.\n\nSERVICES\n\nWater from a local group water scheme, drainage to a septic tank, mains electricity.\n"
      },
